{:edb/db-before-t 2870 :edb/db-after-t 2871 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536183 50 #inst "2026-10-09T18:36:22.797Z" 13194139536183 true] [17592186119579 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14059450/assets/2a24a49f0fc47c235776597df655e75be9c68cffbb7988db16b36d9200f801bc.png)" 13194139536183 false] [17592186119579 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083348/assets/2989739b62112c05f49beb975eb9039d1bbc7fca39ffd4d0adc058c7cf1cbb41.png)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387645 13194139536183 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387652 13194139536183 true] [17592186119760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387687 13194139536183 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387666 13194139536183 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387673 13194139536183 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387680 13194139536183 true] [17592186119761 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387701 13194139536183 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387659 13194139536183 true] [17592186119762 1020 #edb/ref 17592186387694 13194139536183 true] [17592186120162 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536183 true] [17592186120162 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩=19.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186120162 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$l: \\frac{x - 1}{2} = \\frac{y + 2}{1} = \\frac{z - 1}{3}, Π: r \\cdot ⟨1, 6, 2⟩ = 19$." 13194139536183 false] [17592186120162 1145 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,1,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,0,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387646 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1089 "q-108309" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1113 #uuid "310a805e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387645 1145 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387647 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387648 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387649 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387650 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387651 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387647 13194139536183 true] [17592186387646 1110 #uuid "67b7fb82-dedf-5df6-810f-b039da558d9d" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387647 1034 "(1,5,2)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387647 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387647 1111 #uuid "02335c7f-58d3-594e-9025-e77d2b6b1f89" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387648 1034 "(3,5,-4)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387648 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387648 1111 #uuid "f9506b63-8fa9-5c67-b86c-a3f87456ee92" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387649 1034 "(0,7,5)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387649 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387649 1111 #uuid "566d37e9-07ac-568b-b305-b71b19df247c" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387650 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387650 1111 #uuid "5fda1781-0421-56f4-a55a-476bf2136d75" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387651 1034 "(3,1,-4)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387651 1111 #uuid "d7fd3367-5165-591e-a1c4-d798c3288854" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387653 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1089 "q-108310" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,3,0⟩+t⟨3,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩=-19.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1113 #uuid "8e5fe668-3628-59a7-b261-da619f1e8497" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387652 1145 "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)+1(3-2t)-3t & =-19 \\\\ -8+12t+3-2t-3t & =-19 \\\\ 7t & =-14 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(-2),3-2(-2),(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-8,7,-2).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387654 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387655 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387656 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387657 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387658 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387658 13194139536183 true] [17592186387653 1110 #uuid "cb2ddc0f-27fb-57ab-b8fc-48c5d3b48be2" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387654 1034 "(1,-1,1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387654 1111 #uuid "98729640-d11c-57fe-b316-27485116f69d" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387655 1034 "(-2,3,0)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387655 1111 #uuid "ae8eb77c-6b88-5cfe-b984-034b6b32d4bc" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387656 1034 "(-5,5,-1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387656 1111 #uuid "136cb6b5-7e4a-5eb7-98f5-004f40e9e211" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387657 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387657 1111 #uuid "aa2791b2-66c4-5ec5-8735-1e18b0d843b9" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387658 1034 "(-8,7,-2)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387658 1111 #uuid "2ccb4777-a636-5447-a5d9-f3ab9b925214" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387660 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1089 "q-108325" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1113 #uuid "5e78c76d-4b0c-5299-a8c9-57ef8fd9ba3e" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387659 1145 "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387661 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387662 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387663 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387664 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387665 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387661 13194139536183 true] [17592186387660 1110 #uuid "dbdd719a-4878-57c6-bcfd-7fa1eae01e15" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387661 1034 "(-4,-1,8)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387661 1111 #uuid "b6af5075-3f00-5b3e-b98d-3caab5a37adb" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387662 1034 "(2,-3,4)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387662 1111 #uuid "6850bd1d-b068-5f7b-8fee-72a5ed76e4aa" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387663 1034 "(-1,-2,6)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387663 1111 #uuid "9dc699a6-ddfd-5104-bda8-ad435c6ee34f" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387664 1034 "(5,-4,2)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387664 1111 #uuid "23d56610-6a2a-5a66-b792-2a883a6e0483" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387665 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387665 1111 #uuid "dd475f9c-5c3d-537a-a0c0-e7d3e2e12d11" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387667 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1089 "q-108371" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨10,-5,12⟩+s⟨4,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,5⟩.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1113 #uuid "0da8771f-0983-5e77-be97-afe167de38df" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387666 1145 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vector to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨4,3,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =15i-20j+8k \\\\  & =⟨15,-20,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =⟨10,-5,12⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ ⟨4+5w,-2-w,3+2w⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ 15(4+5w)-20(-2-w)+8(3+2w) & =346 \\\\ 60+75w+40+20w+24+16w & =346 \\\\ 111w & =222 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨4+5(2),-2-(2),3+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14,-4,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(14,-4,7).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387668 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387669 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387670 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387671 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387672 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387672 13194139536183 true] [17592186387667 1110 #uuid "8269ff46-ca04-5b2b-b137-fa58cf5a3d69" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387668 1034 "(9,-3,5)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387668 1111 #uuid "e7d6e3a2-bd17-518b-a420-9be2d6ede2d0" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387669 1034 "(-1,-1,1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387669 1111 #uuid "fd1e7486-194c-5f91-b648-30d5fc905ddc" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387670 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387670 1111 #uuid "3142852d-48b8-5774-8470-a6efcf238212" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387671 1034 "(-6,0,-1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387671 1111 #uuid "bf61788e-b726-5e47-a6a7-89955c7d41db" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387672 1034 "(14,-4,7)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387672 1111 #uuid "0db1fcb0-c0a8-57e5-ac80-2d73a1e639ad" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387674 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1089 "q-108889" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1113 #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387673 1145 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387675 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387676 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387677 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387678 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387679 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387677 13194139536183 true] [17592186387674 1110 #uuid "46fdd381-d1f3-5a54-b9a2-08fb1c4a79c0" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387675 1034 "(13,7,2)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387675 1111 #uuid "d6d831ac-92de-5fef-b4b6-09d774020b60" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387676 1034 "(8,3,-1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387676 1111 #uuid "f70f6d86-43fd-59f7-a0fb-b400b5d7e414" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387677 1034 "(-12,-5,-13)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387677 1111 #uuid "6fba1001-8369-5c0e-95f6-7fdb50afa8e4" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387678 1034 "(-7,-3,-10)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387678 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387678 1111 #uuid "67e25cb5-4491-5247-b689-ce094bd09db1" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387679 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387679 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387679 1111 #uuid "0380037d-3624-5985-af69-76df39ab115c" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387681 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1089 "q-33197" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-2}{-3}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{-1},\\,Π:3x-2y+z-38=0.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1113 #uuid "f5c58476-2e22-55a5-af93-3aace6df8e02" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387680 1145 "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(2,3,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-3,2,-1⟩.$ Therefore, its parametric equations are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,3,-4⟩+t⟨-3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+z-38 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+z & =38 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ ⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ 3(2-3t)-2(3+2t)+(-4-t) & =38 \\\\ 6-9t-6-4t-4-t & =38 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-3(-3),3+2(-3),-4-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(11,-3,-1).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387682 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387683 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387684 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387685 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387686 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387686 13194139536183 true] [17592186387681 1110 #uuid "c8ac8054-65d2-5274-b462-4accb5725bdc" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387682 1034 "(1,-3,-11)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387682 1111 #uuid "f0b88eff-8ed7-5763-8342-49fe491b68cf" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387683 1034 "(11,-1,-3)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387683 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387683 1111 #uuid "719be12e-1496-55f2-b6c2-e488693d6fe8" 13194