d $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y+5z-85 & =0 \\\\ -3(-2-t)+2(9-3t)+5(-1-6t) & =85 \\\\ 6+3t+18-6t-5-30t & =85 \\\\ -33t & =66 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2-(-2)=0 \\\\ y=9-3(-2)=15 \\\\ z=-1-6(-2)=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(0,15,11).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387696 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387697 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387698 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387699 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387700 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1041 "selection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387700 13194139536183 true] [17592186387695 1110 #uuid "f8c4ab64-c79a-5f27-acbd-ad32ba576566" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387696 1034 "(10,12,11)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387696 1111 #uuid "7315de20-0bee-54fa-a72e-d1aa9d3084e7" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387697 1034 "(1,0,1)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387697 1111 #uuid "00e01c5b-2f3c-55e8-bdde-89c15e05ec2b" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387698 1034 "No intersection" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536183 true] [17592186387698 1111 #uuid "5c5047ab-818b-52c9-b2eb-3ea7c3c64f63" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387699 1034 "(0,3,11)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387699 1111 #uuid "01005393-fe01-5dbd-b6d9-06e68c1a5e4d" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387700 1034 "(0,15,11)" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536183 true] [17592186387700 1111 #uuid "63885195-7515-59db-91dd-619141f62808" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387702 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1089 "q-74004" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1100 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1113 #uuid "845a9150-4e19-5e0f-8a87-b8822d534204" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387701 1145 "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$" 13194139536183 true] [17592186387702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387703 13194139